WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.069 --> 00:00:05.278
Hey, what's up guys and welcome to the old hunters DLC. It's finally here!

00:00:05.279 --> 00:00:08.369
I think I've played through about a quarter of it so far

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:13.740
and I just want to share that hunt with you. New weapons, new bosses, new NPC's. And,

00:00:14.769 --> 00:00:20.128
hopefully a new understanding of the hunters who were around when the hunt first began.

00:00:20.439 --> 00:00:24.209
So let's hunt through it all together and let's see what we can find

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:28.980
Defeat Vicar Amelia and the Messengers will bring you two items

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:36.720
first, the eye of a blood-drunk hunter. The pupil has collapsed here which indicates the onset of the scourge of beasts a

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:40.800
Hunter who goes drunk with blood is said to be taken by the Hunters nightmare

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.480
Destined to Wander forever engaged in an endless

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:49.230
nightmarish hunt...no Hunter can Escape this fate apparently.

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:54.809
The second item is the old Hunter Bell countless Hunters have passed through the dream

00:00:54.809 --> 00:00:57.029
but cannot forget the 'thrill of the hunt'

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:03.749
The messengers relay these thoughts and if you ring the bell by their side then the hunters are sure to listen

00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:06.299
for the night of the hunt is long and

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:12.419
Unchanging and this bell closes the gap between worlds with these items in your inventory

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:19.559
The Amygdala outside Cathedral Ward will take you to the Old Hunters Nightmare, but unlike the old Hunters before us

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:22.650
We go there as a hunter who has not completely

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:30.390
Succumbed to bloodlust. That's not what sucked us in what sucked us in was this creature that we know is capable of teleporting you

00:01:31.299 --> 00:01:35.368
curse the fiends..their children too and

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:39.419
their children forever true.

00:01:40.329 --> 00:01:43.859
If there's an answer for that dialogue, I haven't found it yet

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:48.929
I don't know who it belongs to. Who is this woman to place a curse upon people, and

00:01:49.119 --> 00:01:53.309
What curse is she placing? We should remember this for another episode.

00:01:54.189 --> 00:01:58.529
We arrive in a distorted version of Cathedral Ward and it's

00:01:58.780 --> 00:01:59.280
surroundings

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:05.159
And maybe distorted is the wrong word though? To me this area strikes me as badly

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:12.119
remembered. Imagine if you had to construct a place from memory. You wouldn't get it 100% correct would you? and

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:19.439
To me, I kind of like to think that whatever hosts this nightmare had trouble remembering the towers in the distance

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:23.159
so the Towers appear tilted and illogical and

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:30.150
Gaps in memory are replaced by these rocky hills where there should be man-made paths instead

00:02:30.819 --> 00:02:35.908
But this world, this nightmare. It's inhabited, just like all the others were you know Micolash's

00:02:35.909 --> 00:02:37.909
nightmare was inhabited by the

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:44.009
Puppets that he pulled into the nightmare with him and also by random Hunters who made their way in as well

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:47.789
The Geography might be a reconstruction from somebody's memory

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:49.750
But the people within it

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:52.829
Aren't. This nightmare is full of Old Hunters.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:03:00.719
Some of the first people to ever fight against the beasts in the first hunts that ever happened. Hunters who according to the eye

00:03:01.299 --> 00:03:08.999
"Lost themselves to bloodlust and were pulled into a nightmare where the hunt never ends" and this shows in the gameplay

00:03:09.069 --> 00:03:14.938
The Hunters and the beasts here are constantly fighting one another and you can use that to your advantage

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:17.909
The beasts are weak compared to the Hunters

00:03:17.919 --> 00:03:23.849
but there are so many! So I like to take out the hunters while they're distracted with the beasts and

00:03:24.099 --> 00:03:29.578
Once you're done with the hunters. You can equip a torch and deal with the beasts. They'll rarely attack you

00:03:30.549 --> 00:03:36.328
All of these hunters are wielding weapons and wearing a guard that isn't seen in Modern-day

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:43.619
Yharnam you'll find pieces of their equipment throughout the early level and the old hunter garb in particular is funny, its

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:50.729
Description details the superstitions of the first Hunters how some hunters believed that the "Beastly plague

00:03:50.859 --> 00:03:56.638
Crept up the right leg" so they wrapped a bit of belt around the right leg of their trousers

00:03:57.250 --> 00:04:02.759
Some thought that bits of metal on their gloves could ward away the beast's blood and...you get the picture

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:05.030
They were superstitious bunch back then

00:04:05.769 --> 00:04:13.019
The just beast tells us that: "one day the hunters disappeared drunk with blood they would pass onto the nightmare

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:16.829
Every last one of them." I wonder what's pulling them in?

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:23.820
Regardless, these hunters were around in the first days of the hunt and this nightmare contains people and the places that

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:25.919
existed when the hunt first began

00:04:25.919 --> 00:04:33.389
And I really think that inside it, we'll find the answer to what started the hunt, and why. On this little crop of land

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:36.779
We find our first new weapon, which is the Beast Cutter

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:42.360
it's like a crude more brutal version of the Threaded Cane. The weapon is described as:

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:49.260
"Regrettably inelegant", which suggests that the earliest hunts were clumsy and Bloody and brutal which

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:51.809
Certainly wouldn't have helped these hunters

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:53.460
resist the bloodshed.

00:04:53.460 --> 00:05:00.660
Perhaps the refinement of weapons wasn't just so you could deal with beasts efficiently, it would be so you could deal with them more cleanly

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:06.899
Anyway, the world here is full of Twin Bloodstone and later Bloodstone Chunks as well,

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:13.380
so if you want to choose a new weapon to upgrade, it could easily be one of these you find in the early DLC and

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:17.580
the DLC continuously bombards you with new weapons,

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:23.280
which I really like. It's not like the core game that gives you all the cool weapons at the very end

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:27.450
There are some good weapons at the very start of this DLC, and you find a new one

00:05:27.450 --> 00:05:30.420
What feels like...every 15 minutes or so.

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:39.119
So far, most of my enemies have been humanoid not beasts, or monsters so as a result I definitely recommend the blunderbuss

00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:41.110
Over something like the pistol.

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:46.589
I've always found that the pistol misses too much against human enemies, like you can't riposte them very well

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:52.649
so you might want to go with the blunderbuss...and I find the blunderbuss is better at taking out all the Hunters and

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:55.200
If I'm making this look easy

00:05:55.200 --> 00:06:01.229
it's because I've been through here before! I accidentally played through all of this stage on a new game+

00:06:01.570 --> 00:06:07.710
Character and holy shit this area in new game+ is tough enemies have so many more hit points

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:13.980
I actually got up to the first boss on my new game+ character and completely forgot that I was in new game+

00:06:14.230 --> 00:06:16.980
But the first boss really reminded me of that.

00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:23.219
I still haven't beaten the first boss on my new game+ character, and I was going to show you guys that playthrough

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:26.160
But my PC decided to corrupt the footage instead

00:06:26.230 --> 00:06:31.559
So this character who is not in new Game+ is so much easier by comparison.

00:06:32.380 --> 00:06:36.450
My recommendation to you guys is: that if you have a new game+ character,

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:43.110
And if it's below level 60, like mine was don't expect to get the first boss without a hell of a fight.

00:06:43.350 --> 00:06:49.770
Choose your character wisely...and look! It's the Cleric Beast! Here comes a boss fight right? ...Any second now

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:56.939
Okay, maybe it starts when I pick up the item? No? No okay, then maybe it starts when I leave? No?

00:06:56.940 --> 00:06:59.490
It doesn't? ..Didn't expect that. Maybe later?

00:07:00.070 --> 00:07:07.170
Anyway, the Eye Pendant the Cleric Beast was holding reads: "Unlocks the surgery altar." The next weapon

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:08.730
We find is the Boom Hammer

00:07:08.730 --> 00:07:09.130
and

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:14.369
It's waiting for you in front of this old guy, who is the guy that shoots you when you pick up the item in front

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:18.600
Of him. I'm sure you all remember that trap...I was like: "You're not gonna' fool me again!" Oh...

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:21.240
This is different.

00:07:23.590 --> 00:07:28.019
The interesting part of this weapon reads: "Crush the beasts then burn them."

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:34.259
The brute simplicity of the Boom Hammer was favoured by Hunters with an acute distaste for beasts

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:41.969
This was crafted by the Powder-Keg Hunters. One of the first hunter groups and a lot of descriptions do reference these groups

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:44.940
Bloodborne already has a fairly straightforward timeline

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:48.900
It's not like Dark Souls which spans hundreds or even thousands of years.

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:54.179
Bloodborne's timeline seems like it happens within a century or so, in my opinion

00:07:54.520 --> 00:08:01.409
so this DLC answers a lot of questions about the progression through all the different hunter groups and their history and

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:07.080
we even learned that there is a group that came before the Powder-Keg Hunters and

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:11.850
It's this beastly enemy we fight next that gives us this information.

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:18.659
He has this enhanced beasthood that I've still yet to learn about he has a way bigger moveset than the Beast Claws

00:08:18.820 --> 00:08:24.179
Should give you. I think it's a rune that lets you get into the beast Form he's in. Anyway

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:32.070
He's where the central Yharnam lamp would be, where Gilbert would be if this was the real world and he drops the Firing Hammer Badge

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:40.109
Which I believe unlocks the timed molotov cocktails that you saw being thrown around before, and also the Piercing Rifle which

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:41.860
was and I quote:

00:08:41.860 --> 00:08:47.760
"Developed by the Oto Workshop, which was the workshop that came before the Powder-Keg Hunter workshop.

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:53.649
"You're a hunter with your sanity aren't you?

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:56.859
Must have taken a wrong turn then, eh?

00:08:57.890 --> 00:09:00.669
Well, we're more alike than you think

00:09:02.149 --> 00:09:04.449
This is the Hunters nightmare

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:08.500
where Hunters end up when drunk with blood.

00:09:09.709 --> 00:09:11.709
You've seen them before?

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:16.300
Aimless wandering Hunters slavering like beasts...

00:09:17.630 --> 00:09:25.089
This is what the poor fools have to look forward to. So! Don't be brash, turn back before it's too late.

00:09:26.630 --> 00:09:29.079
Unless you've something of an interest in nightmares?"

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:38.979
"Yes, as it should be hunt your beasts and think no more on the secrets of the night.

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:42.820
That is the very best a Hunter can do.

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:46.060
Just don't let the blood

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:48.430
intoxicate you."

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:52.269
You can say 'No' here. You can say 'I'm not interested in nightmares.'

00:09:52.610 --> 00:10:00.130
But then, you can also talk to him again to give, what is supposedly the 'right' answer which is apparently: "Yes

00:10:00.130 --> 00:10:03.969
I am interested in nightmares." Because he stops talking to you after you say 'Yes.'

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:10.300
"What now? Oh take my word, and turn back before it's too late.

00:10:12.079 --> 00:10:16.419
Unless I suppose, you've taken an interest in nightmares? ...Oh

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:24.010
Yes, I see. You sense a secret within the nightmare, and cannot bear to leave it be as

00:10:24.649 --> 00:10:31.389
If the spirit of Byrgenwerth lives on within you. Such inquisitive Hunters will relish the nightmare,

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:34.130
but beware

00:10:34.130 --> 00:10:39.519
Secrets, are secrets for a reason and some do not wish to see them uncovered

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:44.609
Especially when the secrets are particularly unseemly."

00:10:45.850 --> 00:10:50.700
This guy will appear later and he tells us to carry on further into the nightmare

00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:54.059
But he warns us that some secrets aren't meant to be found

00:10:54.580 --> 00:10:59.729
Secrets like down the Blood River is the Gatling-Gun hunter who attacks you in the pitch-black

00:11:00.100 --> 00:11:05.159
With this brutal, brutal weapon that will stun-lock you if you stand anywhere near him.

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:10.469
I found the best way was to rotate around this rock until he takes a break from firing

00:11:10.660 --> 00:11:16.350
then you get a few hits in, and you rinse and repeat. His gun can't fire forever, so

00:11:16.630 --> 00:11:19.589
Start your assault on him as soon as it stops firing.

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:25.919
You actually get the Gatling-Gun for defeating him. It requires Blood Tinge and strength

00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:32.219
So I'm going to bet that blood-tinged strength builds are going to be a thing now, that weapon is a beast!

00:11:32.520 --> 00:11:37.499
I really recommend using the Hand Lantern in here further on you have to fight a small

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:38.920
Bloodletting Beast and

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:44.070
You'll actually want to see what you're shooting at, because it's important to counter this guy with a gun in your left hand

00:11:44.440 --> 00:11:50.999
this room holds the Amygdalan arm a gruesome little trick weapon, that you can use as a short hammer or a

00:11:51.490 --> 00:11:56.940
Sinewy-scythe-thing where one of the limbs just flows around with the ligament attached to it

00:11:57.250 --> 00:12:02.039
From is so creative with their weapons! The next two weapons is the Beast Hunter's Saif

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:06.329
Which is way better than I thought it would be it just looks like a short-saw cleaver

00:12:06.339 --> 00:12:10.529
but its simplest attacks include a lot of little dashes, and

00:12:10.899 --> 00:12:15.749
Everyone knows how important it is in souls games to quickly close distances

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:21.779
It's a really underestimated weapon, I think. The next weapon is the Whirligig Saw. I love it,

00:12:21.779 --> 00:12:25.229
just look at how you can grind down an enemy by Holding L2

00:12:25.750 --> 00:12:30.510
this weapon belongs to Valtr, the Beast-Eater, leader of the league and

00:12:30.910 --> 00:12:36.719
He's the old hunter you meet in the Forbidden Woods if you went and joined the League when patch

00:12:37.089 --> 00:12:40.619
1.07 hit. The League is a co-op covenant

00:12:40.620 --> 00:12:44.039
And I'm going to use this guy to help me in my boss fight

00:12:44.260 --> 00:12:47.939
because I found the boss fight really tough I haven't had much sleep, so

00:12:48.490 --> 00:12:50.490
Maybe I'm just not fighting very well

00:12:50.770 --> 00:12:54.600
But it felt good summoning this guy this guy! This DLC is called;

00:12:54.780 --> 00:12:58.620
"The old Hunters" after all and I might as well summon one of them, right?

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:01.500
It was nice feeling like I had a teammate against this guy.

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:04.560
So, let's fight that next boss shall we?

00:13:54.990 --> 00:13:58.190
I'm not going to talk too much about the lore in these videos

00:13:58.350 --> 00:14:06.229
But just quickly, Ludwig was originally the first hunter of the healing church a cleric who became one of the most gruesome

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:08.840
beasts. In the first phase of the fight

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:11.419
It's vitally important that you kind of become

00:14:11.790 --> 00:14:17.570
familiar with his move-set and most importantly I think you have to learn where it's safe to hit him and

00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:22.669
Where it's safe to heal. I find the best place to be attacking is his left side

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:28.789
because if you get behind him he'll buck at you like a horse. If you get under him he'll stamp around and

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:35.269
Likely kill you and if you get in front of him, he'll do these quick little slashes that are hard to predict and dodge.

00:14:35.790 --> 00:14:41.000
Inevitably you do have to dodge through these front facing dashes, and that's what's so tough.

00:14:41.550 --> 00:14:46.880
One of these dashes has a really long wind-up that will catch you if you dodge too early

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:53.840
but you have to dodge early against most of his dashes because they will combo you if you just take the hit, So

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:57.380
It's a tough fight because of that, you can't dodge too early

00:14:57.380 --> 00:15:02.179
And you can't dodge too late. Your reflexes have to be on point if you're soloing this guy

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:09.349
Which is why I brought Valtr in. I decided that this companion Hunter was going to be my 'win' condition

00:15:09.350 --> 00:15:11.350
he's fantastic for

00:15:11.730 --> 00:15:12.930
distracting Ludwig

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:20.030
but he only has a limited amount of blood vessels so once he's healed like five times he'll stop healing and

00:15:20.130 --> 00:15:26.419
The boss will kill him and you'll be in trouble, so like I said my 'win' condition was to keep him alive

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:28.910
I brought the Choir Bell along with me

00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:33.559
And I kept healing Valtr whenever he got low. So basically I was keeping my tank alive,

00:15:33.560 --> 00:15:37.849
I'd never fought a fight like that in Bloodborne before, so this was really fun for me

00:15:37.850 --> 00:15:42.890
And I really wanted this NPC for phase 2 of this fight.

00:16:19.329 --> 00:16:26.789
This is awesome. That music transition is so seamless and epic all of a sudden--Moonlight Greatsword out of nowhere!

00:16:27.129 --> 00:16:31.589
But if you did look closely, you would have noticed that Ludwig actually had this Moonlight Greatsword

00:16:32.110 --> 00:16:34.110
Strapped to his back all along.

00:16:34.149 --> 00:16:39.659
It's fairly easy to dodge the swipes from this Great Sword, if he starts doing slam attacks

00:16:39.660 --> 00:16:43.589
you dodge early, and if he starts swiping you dodge through the attacks and

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:49.769
During this fight, you'll have two chances to riposte him, to perform visceral attacks.

00:16:49.839 --> 00:16:53.368
And it took me a while to figure out where to perform the Visceral attack

00:16:53.470 --> 00:16:56.339
But eventually I realized you have to go right up to his crotch

00:16:56.339 --> 00:17:04.168
and...yeah. The easiest way to die in this fight, is if you get caught in his huge charged-up Moonlight Wave attack

00:17:04.270 --> 00:17:07.770
He does this quick AOE (Area of Effect [attack]) to make you dodge backwards

00:17:07.809 --> 00:17:12.479
But then he follows it up with his slam down that creates this giant wave of moonlight

00:17:12.480 --> 00:17:13.779
energy that just destroys

00:17:13.779 --> 00:17:15.189
you! Look how

00:17:15.189 --> 00:17:20.398
devastating it is! So you've got to dodge away from the initial AOE and then you've got to get right back close to him again

00:17:20.399 --> 00:17:23.069
So you can dodge that attack, but eventually...

00:17:23.589 --> 00:17:25.589
...I succeeded.

